description: CLI source for command parsing, compile orchestration, ToolForge, and diagnostic rendering
includes:
  - crates/sigil-cli/src/
excludes:
  - crates/sigil-cli/target/
context: |
  This scope is the implementation-level view of the CLI.
  Keep it thin: parse arguments, call compiler/runtime APIs, and present
  diagnostics or compile results clearly.

  Avoid reimplementing language semantics here; if a rule belongs to parsing or
  type checking, push it back into `sigil-compiler`.

  The current CLI has three orchestration roles:
  - compile/check and runtime boot for full Sigil modules
  - ToolForge compilation and ephemeral execution with grants and fuel controls
  - template-registry management over `sigil-registry`

  It should keep translating user intent into compiler/runtime/registry API calls
  without rebuilding shared runtime metadata or accumulating host-state logic of
  its own.
related:
  - crates/sigil-cli/.scope
  - crates/sigil-abi/.scope
  - crates/sigil-compiler/.scope
  - crates/sigil-registry/.scope
tags:
  - cli
  - src
  - diagnostics
  - toolforge
